Dialogue: 10,0:00:01.02,0:00:06.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I think my dad couldn't \Nhandle being labeled a thief.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:06.06,0:00:11.08,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,My mom apparently thought\Nhe really did steal it, too.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:12.04,0:00:14.71,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It made me want to stop believing in people.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:15.22,0:00:21.14,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I even thought that maybe I'd feel better\Nif I ended up hating one of my parents.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:21.14,0:00:28.56,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,But years later, my mom let slip that she\Nregretted not believing him back then.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:29.35,0:00:34.44,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That's when I realized I should\Ncontinue to love them both.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:37.11,0:00:42.03,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I realized that my belief in people \Nwas one of the good things about me.
Dialogue: 10,0:02:14.50,0:02:16.88,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wh-What the hell?
Dialogue: 10,0:02:16.88,0:02:19.13,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I saw Airi-chan go in there!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:19.13,0:02:21.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,C-Could she still be inside?
Dialogue: 10,0:02:21.60,0:02:22.22,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:25.77,0:02:26.64,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Airi!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:27.95,0:02:29.75,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Can you hear me, Airi?
Dialogue: 10,0:02:30.77,0:02:31.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Airi!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:37.77,0:02:38.76,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Airi!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:40.35,0:02:41.36,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hang in there!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:49.51,0:02:50.41,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's heavy!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:58.02,0:02:59.94,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hey, Airi!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:02.44,0:03:03.49,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:04.05,0:03:06.18,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's no way I can do this!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:08.55,0:03:09.49,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Manager?
Dialogue: 10,0:03:09.49,0:03:11.75,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You should never count on a comic artist, huh?
Dialogue: 10,0:03:12.72,0:03:14.73,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,We're going down in one go!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:21.63,0:03:24.26,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Satoru, go out the back.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:24.99,0:03:26.95,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Don't get Airi-kun mixed up in this anymore.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:33.66,0:03:35.75,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm taking all the credit!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:45.01,0:03:46.76,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will Airi be okay?
Dialogue: 10,0:03:47.62,0:03:49.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But that fire...
Dialogue: 10,0:03:49.60,0:03:52.45,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't tell me he was behind it as well.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:53.54,0:03:54.43,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, right!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:57.78,0:04:00.30,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He set the fire to try to kill Airi.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:00.30,0:04:02.53,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And it looks like I did it.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:03.18,0:04:06.70,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Airi snuck her phone into my pocket\Nso the police wouldn't see this text.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:07.53,0:04:13.00,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means the killer already knew\NAiri's address, or he followed her.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:14.64,0:04:17.07,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He might be closer than I thought.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:17.71,0:04:19.35,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to look for him.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:19.35,0:04:23.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Either I find him, or I get caught trying.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:33.79,0:04:34.64,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 10,0:04:36.19,0:04:39.10,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Who is this? Identify yourself.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:39.87,0:04:41.32,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Fujinuma Satoru.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:43.32,0:04:46.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,If you really are Fujinuma Satoru,\Nthen it's a pleasure.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:46.60,0:04:49.03,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for your call.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:49.63,0:04:51.00,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:51.00,0:04:54.49,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Not here, though. Let's meet somewhere else.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:55.13,0:04:58.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Right, I haven't introduced myself yet.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:58.16,0:04:59.92,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Let's save that for when we meet tomorrow.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:00.79,0:05:05.25,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Because you might be the one \Nwho murdered Fujinuma Sachiko.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:08.62,0:05:09.84,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Welcome!
Dialogue: 10,0:05:11.62,0:05:14.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hey, Satoru-kun. Over here.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:14.86,0:05:15.84,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:15.84,0:05:18.91,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm Sawada, formerly of the TV Ishikari city desk.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:18.91,0:05:21.56,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness. You really are Satoru-kun.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:22.14,0:05:24.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you resemble your mother.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:27.36,0:05:28.28,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,{\i1}It's him.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:28.70,0:05:32.41,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Since you're probably wondering:\Nno, I didn't tip off the cops.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:32.41,0:05:35.09,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I didn't murder your mother, either.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:35.64,0:05:37.73,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You don't suspect me?
Dialogue: 10,0:05:37.73,0:05:39.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:39.19,0:05:40.25,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 10,0:05:41.71,0:05:46.21,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Because a mother like her \Nwouldn't have raised a murderer.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:47.16,0:05:48.42,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:48.42,0:05:51.68,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I remembered yesterday that I had it in my pocket.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:52.40,0:05:54.59,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,This has become quite a conundrum.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:55.35,0:05:56.89,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I have no excuse.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:56.89,0:06:00.89,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's also partly my fault since I keep screwing up.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:00.89,0:06:05.23,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's pointless to blame yourself\Nfor something after it happens.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:06.15,0:06:08.28,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Sachiko-san's words.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:08.28,0:06:09.86,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I always liked them.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:13.47,0:06:15.87,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Shall we talk about what I discussed\Nover the phone with her?
Dialogue: 10,0:06:16.64,0:06:17.87,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yes, please.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:18.82,0:06:23.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Sawada-kun, do you remember the\Nserial murder case from 18 years ago?
Dialogue: 10,0:06:23.83,0:06:28.63,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Of course. Shiratori Jun is on death row,\Nbut he still hasn't admitted his guilt.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:28.63,0:06:31.20,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Satoru was right about it.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:31.80,0:06:33.84,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Shiratori-kun didn't do it.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:34.53,0:06:36.85,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,I've realized who the real culprit is.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:37.75,0:06:39.32,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Let's meet at Koiwa Station tomorrow.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:40.58,0:06:42.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I should've asked for a name.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:46.91,0:06:50.32,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,There's a past incident I want to discuss.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:50.32,0:06:52.86,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The murder of Hinazuki Kayo-chan.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:53.68,0:06:56.71,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,On the night of March 2nd, 1988,
Dialogue: 10,0:06:56.71,0:07:01.29,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Kayo was locked in the shed after being beaten up\Nby her mother and her mother's boyfriend.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:01.68,0:07:03.70,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,She froze to death.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:03.70,0:07:09.40,GJM_Main,,15,375,0,,At first, the police suspected the mother\N and her boyfriend, thinking they'd hid the body.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:10.02,0:07:16.09,GJM_Main,,15,375,0,,But in reality, Kayo disappeared from the shed\Nsometime between 10 and 11 p.m. on the 2nd.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:16.57,0:07:20.35,GJM_Main,,15,375,0,,When her mother noticed she \Nwas gone at 12:30 a.m. on the 3rd,
Dialogue: 10,0:07:20.35,0:07:24.31,GJM_Main,,15,600,0,,she called your house and nonchalantly\Ninquired about Kayo's whereabouts.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:26.17,0:07:28.51,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It was Shiratori Jun who had kidnapped her.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:28.51,0:07:32.94,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,One piece of evidence provided was that\Nthe rubber boot prints made near the shed
Dialogue: 10,0:07:32.94,0:07:35.05,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,matched with boots found at the Shiratori home.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:36.89,0:07:39.81,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The official version of events is as follows.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:39.81,0:07:43.75,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He knocked her out with\N blunt force, photographed her,
Dialogue: 10,0:07:44.45,0:07:49.18,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,and took her to a commercial freezer, \Nwhere he used a spray to speed up her death.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:49.18,0:07:51.89,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,When her body temperature dropped\Nto 20 degrees, she was brain-dead.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:52.64,0:07:56.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,He then waited 30 minutes \Nto eliminate any chance of survival
Dialogue: 10,0:07:57.00,0:08:00.50,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,and returned the corpse to the\NHinazuki's shed before sunrise.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:06.10,0:08:08.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yuuki-san would never do something like that!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:08.64,0:08:14.72,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,A little before Hinazuki Kayo, \NSugita Hiromi and Nakanishi Aya disappeared,
Dialogue: 10,0:08:14.72,0:08:18.31,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,there were serial kidnapping and \Nmurder cases in the next town over too.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:18.31,0:08:23.20,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The culprit was caught immediately and,\Njust like Shiratori, denied any wrongdoing.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:23.64,0:08:29.29,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Now, if we take your current predicament\Ninto account, do you notice a pattern?
Dialogue: 10,0:08:31.60,0:08:37.59,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,People keep ridiculing me as a crazy reporter\Nwho investigates closed cases.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:38.05,0:08:40.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,But in reality, none of these cases are closed.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:40.47,0:08:45.93,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Hinazuki Kayo and Sachiko were both killed\Nby a man who frames others for his crimes!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:47.06,0:08:49.85,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,And he's in this city right now.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:49.85,0:08:52.26,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He's one tricky bastard.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:52.26,0:08:55.42,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,By creating additional suspects,\Nhe delays the investigation,
Dialogue: 10,0:08:55.42,0:08:58.90,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,causing eyewitness testimonies to diminish\Nand the crime scene to deteriorate.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:59.27,0:09:02.36,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,As a result, the trail to him goes cold.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:14.47,0:09:16.03,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Talk about overreacting.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:19.75,0:09:22.79,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,So Fujinuma Satoru tried to silence her?
Dialogue: 10,0:09:22.79,0:09:25.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He won't be able to get at her now.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:25.55,0:09:27.80,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,But what about her?
Dialogue: 10,0:09:27.80,0:09:29.17,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Is she an accomplice?
Dialogue: 10,0:09:29.17,0:09:33.56,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He forced her to help him kill his mother, \Nand once that was done, he tried to silence her.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:33.94,0:09:37.56,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,How awful. I can't believe he dragged\Nthe girl into his mess like that.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:38.14,0:09:39.14,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're wrong.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:40.05,0:09:42.82,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,There's no need for you to apologize, Airi-chan.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:42.82,0:09:48.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah. It was all that stalker's fault, \Nnot yours. You must've been so scared.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:48.47,0:09:50.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That's not what happened, Auntie.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:50.16,0:09:54.38,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's okay! I'm sorry we didn't notice anything.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:54.38,0:09:55.35,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're wrong.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:55.35,0:09:59.30,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The police are searching for the culprit.\NThere's nothing to be afraid of now.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:00.07,0:10:01.55,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've got it all wrong.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:12.27,0:10:17.02,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't believe they're going after\NSatoru-san for murder and arson.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:18.58,0:10:21.53,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who would believe me...
Dialogue: 10,0:10:28.52,0:10:31.46,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That girl got a text from Sachiko-san's phone?
Dialogue: 10,0:10:31.46,0:10:32.55,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:32.55,0:10:36.54,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The news said she suffered light injuries,\Nbut she's probably still in the hospital.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:36.99,0:10:37.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Here's her phone.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:40.20,0:10:41.58,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:41.58,0:10:45.71,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He tried to help the murder investigation\Nalong by framing you for arson.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:46.30,0:10:50.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm sure that's partly why, \Nbut I was already the prime suspect.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:50.60,0:10:55.70,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I don't think he'd go after her,\NKatagiri Airi, for just that reason.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:55.70,0:10:58.90,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Are you saying she was a target herself?
Dialogue: 10,0:10:59.42,0:11:05.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,In order to frame me for my mother's murder,\Nhe needed to know when I'd get home from work.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:05.53,0:11:11.12,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,He killed her a little more than a day\Nafter she saw his kidnapping attempt.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:11.61,0:11:15.21,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,In that time frame, he visited \Nthe restaurant and saw our shift schedule.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:15.21,0:11:18.85,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,And Airi must've seen him then.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:18.85,0:11:21.30,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He might be someone I know too.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:21.30,0:11:27.02,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\q2}I see. So he's someone who'd be able to get behind\Nthe counter in a store to look at the schedule.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:27.63,0:11:30.89,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,We might be able to use this to get to him.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:31.44,0:11:33.02,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm going to the hospital.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:33.02,0:11:34.39,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,O-Okay.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:34.79,0:11:38.34,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,There are reports on the murders\Nfrom 18 years ago on my computer.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:38.34,0:11:39.77,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Have a look.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:41.53,0:11:46.57,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I theorize that Shiratori Jun suspects\Nhis own father of being the culprit.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:47.15,0:11:52.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's possible that he refuses to provide any alibis\Nor evidence because it may incriminate his father,
Dialogue: 10,0:11:52.16,0:11:54.95,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,but in turn it makes it worse for himself.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:54.95,0:11:57.12,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sounds like Yuuki-san, all right. He loved his dad.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:57.12,0:12:03.05,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Students from school had seen Hinazuki Kayo \Nand Shiratori Jun together on numerous occasions.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:03.05,0:12:05.55,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Fujinuma Satoru's testimony was ignored,
Dialogue: 10,0:12:05.55,0:12:08.49,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,but the testimonies of the other students were taken into serious consideration.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:10.10,0:12:11.68,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A list of suspects?
Dialogue: 10,0:12:11.68,0:12:14.45,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know any of these names\N aside from Yuuki-san and his father.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:14.45,0:12:16.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not to mention, there were only five?
Dialogue: 10,0:12:16.53,0:12:22.53,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The police presumed that Sugita Hiromi\Nwas killed after being mistaken for a girl.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:22.53,0:12:27.99,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,As a result, the police made a list of five suspects\Nwho weren't acquainted with Sugita Hiromi.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:29.90,0:12:31.70,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,We're doing a folk dance today.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:31.70,0:12:33.66,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Seriously?
Dialogue: 10,0:12:33.66,0:12:35.89,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,I don't wanna hold hands with some ugly girl.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:35.89,0:12:38.17,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,I'd much rather have Hiromi!
Dialogue: 10,0:12:38.17,0:12:40.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,Y-You've got guts!
Dialogue: 10,0:12:40.06,0:12:42.63,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,{\i1}It's now clear why Hiromi was killed.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:43.08,0:12:45.31,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The culprit was perfectly aware of his gender,
Dialogue: 10,0:12:45.31,0:12:49.97,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so he killed him to avoid \Nbeing on the list of suspects.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:50.89,0:12:56.53,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Shiratori Jun was arrested after \Nsomeone in the neighborhood reported
Dialogue: 10,0:12:56.53,0:12:59.38,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,that he had been talking to \Na third-grade girl who was alone.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:59.38,0:13:04.87,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Photos taken at the time of Sugita's murder\Nwere found in Shiratori Foods' storeroom,
Dialogue: 10,0:13:04.87,0:13:09.99,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,and the police concluded that \NShiratori Jun had pedophilic tendencies.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:09.99,0:13:14.27,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,They also seized pedophilic\Nmagazines from his room.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:14.27,0:13:15.45,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He never had stuff like that!
Dialogue: 10,0:13:16.21,0:13:19.42,GJM_Main,,0,0,143,,{\i1}All of it was planted by the killer \Nto draw attention away from himself!
Dialogue: 10,0:13:20.29,0:13:22.13,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where's the list from before Hiromi's death?
Dialogue: 10,0:13:23.06,0:13:25.42,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The killer's name must be on it!
Dialogue: 10,0:13:27.58,0:13:29.35,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Katagiri, I'm coming in.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:32.51,0:13:36.35,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Uh, I'm here to visit.\N But first, is the restroom that way?
Dialogue: 10,0:13:36.35,0:13:37.23,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:38.54,0:13:42.77,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No vacancies... except for room 201.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:42.77,0:13:44.34,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,She's asleep.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:44.34,0:13:45.34,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:45.34,0:13:47.13,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Shit! I'm gonna wet myself!
Dialogue: 10,0:13:52.37,0:13:55.58,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Pardon my intrusion, Katagiri Airi-san.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:56.25,0:13:59.26,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Looks like you're not Fujinuma Satoru-san.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:59.91,0:14:03.31,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I-I'm not. I'm Sawada, his friend.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:06.34,0:14:08.17,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Pleased to meet you.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:08.17,0:14:10.01,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm Airi's mother.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:13.74,0:14:16.22,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,There's no way Satoru-san did it.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:16.59,0:14:18.41,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He didn't kill his mother.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:18.41,0:14:20.10,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He didn't try to kill me in a fire, either.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:20.10,0:14:23.93,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He actually came to save me from the fire!
Dialogue: 10,0:14:23.93,0:14:26.74,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Your manager was the one who saved you.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:26.74,0:14:29.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You must be confused \Nafter inhaling all that smoke.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:29.47,0:14:32.40,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I don't know what you've been told,
Dialogue: 10,0:14:32.40,0:14:35.00,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,but they think I could be his accomplice!
Dialogue: 10,0:14:35.60,0:14:38.78,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It hurts me so much that nobody believes me.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:39.35,0:14:43.54,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,But people are even less likely to \Nbelieve Satoru-san, and that hurts me more.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:44.69,0:14:45.68,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Airi.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:46.47,0:14:51.09,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Even now, I still feel like\N I should've gone after your father.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:55.36,0:14:56.72,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,So off you go.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:56.72,0:14:59.79,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, I believe you.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:09.86,0:15:13.32,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Damn! I forgot to turn it off!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:19.66,0:15:22.11,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It was still on! Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:22.11,0:15:22.96,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Is that you, Airi?
Dialogue: 10,0:15:23.47,0:15:24.61,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 10,0:15:24.61,0:15:26.66,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'm fine now.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:26.66,0:15:29.79,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That aside, can we meet at\Nthe usual place right now?
Dialogue: 10,0:15:29.79,0:15:32.82,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,No, stay away! If you do that, you'll get—
Dialogue: 10,0:15:32.82,0:15:35.46,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's all good! I promise I'll come alone!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:39.01,0:15:41.22,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Go! Is it actually gonna fly?
Dialogue: 10,0:15:43.41,0:15:45.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't believe I actually came.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:45.47,0:15:48.95,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I could've just asked her about\Nthe killer over the phone.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:49.78,0:15:53.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It'll only make things worse for her\Nif she gets involved any further.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:55.87,0:15:59.11,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,What? It doesn't fly at all!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:59.11,0:16:02.39,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,That's weird. Why won't it fly?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:03.99,0:16:07.37,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Doing this gives it what's called "aerodynamic lift."
Dialogue: 10,0:16:07.73,0:16:10.30,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Will that really make it fly?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:10.30,0:16:11.29,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:13.92,0:16:16.38,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Whoa! You're right!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:17.48,0:16:18.78,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It flew towards the river!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:20.17,0:16:21.84,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's flying too far!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:20.89,0:16:23.44,GJM_Overlap,,0,0,0,,What's he doing at this hour?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:23.44,0:16:25.40,GJM_Overlap,,0,0,0,,Is he unemployed?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:25.40,0:16:29.13,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did Yuuki-san go through this, too?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:02.75,0:17:04.30,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Here I am, Satoru-san.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:05.04,0:17:05.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:05.60,0:17:08.35,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I came alone, just like I promised!
Dialogue: 10,0:17:08.35,0:17:08.96,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:09.60,0:17:13.04,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I feel bad for worrying that this\Nmight have been a police trap.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:14.31,0:17:15.54,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I said that out loud...
Dialogue: 10,0:17:17.40,0:17:21.58,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You damn well should be worried about that!\NYou're a fugitive, you know.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:22.28,0:17:25.53,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,But I'm happy you believed in me.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:26.02,0:17:26.63,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:28.48,0:17:29.70,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The store?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:30.14,0:17:32.80,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I think that Nishizono guy is the most suspicious.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:32.80,0:17:33.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Nishizono?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:33.83,0:17:35.43,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I've seen him a couple times.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:35.43,0:17:37.72,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The manager treats him with respect,
Dialogue: 10,0:17:37.72,0:17:39.96,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,and from the badge he wears,\Nhe's probably a city councilor.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:39.96,0:17:42.82,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He would've been able to check the schedule,
Dialogue: 10,0:17:42.82,0:17:44.97,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,and it wouldn't be a stretch \Nfor him to know where we live.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:45.40,0:17:47.04,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I've even exchanged pleasantries with him.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:47.56,0:17:51.79,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nishizono? I didn't see that name\Non the list. Could it be an alias?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:51.79,0:17:54.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But surely you can't sit on \Nthe city council using an alias.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:54.60,0:17:57.94,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He probably tried to kill me \Nbecause I know what he looks like.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:57.94,0:18:00.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Damn it! It's not coming together!
Dialogue: 10,0:18:00.61,0:18:02.51,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The final piece of the puzzle won't fit!
Dialogue: 10,0:18:03.07,0:18:07.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Satoru-san, I understand how you feel,\Nbut you can't beat yourself up over it.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:08.55,0:18:11.72,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I have unfinished business from a long time ago.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:12.56,0:18:15.83,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Oh, I'm talking about a story\Nfor a comic I came up with.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:16.22,0:18:20.55,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's a story about a reaper who makes \Na scheduling error and ends up killing a child.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:20.97,0:18:23.00,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He tries desperately to undo his mistake,
Dialogue: 10,0:18:23.00,0:18:28.93,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,but the more he tries, the more misfortune \Nhe brings to the people he comes in contact with.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:29.34,0:18:35.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,He intends to do the right thing, \Nbut everything he does hurts other people.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:39.26,0:18:41.74,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You mean to say he's like you right now?
Dialogue: 10,0:18:42.26,0:18:43.90,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Wouldn't you agree?
Dialogue: 10,0:18:43.90,0:18:44.99,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Are you stupid?
Dialogue: 10,0:18:45.38,0:18:47.12,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Well, I'm not hurt.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:47.12,0:18:50.33,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,And that stuff about other people was\Njust the reaper jumping to conclusions.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:50.33,0:18:53.95,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I think the reaper should have more faith in himself.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:54.49,0:18:58.60,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Everything that's happening \Nright now is just work in progress.
Dialogue: 10,0:18:59.11,0:19:03.46,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,The ending is a ways off, \Nand nobody knows how it'll turn out.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:05.46,0:19:08.55,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm so lucky to have met you, Airi.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:09.95,0:19:11.11,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I said that out loud!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:14.44,0:19:15.77,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You're Fujinuma Satoru, correct?
Dialogue: 10,0:19:19.52,0:19:20.50,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Satoru-san!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:20.50,0:19:21.65,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Stay out of this!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:21.65,0:19:22.86,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Airi!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:25.08,0:19:26.19,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Fujinuma Satoru,
Dialogue: 10,0:19:26.19,0:19:30.64,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,you are under arrest for murder and\Nattempted murder resulting from arson.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:36.10,0:19:38.64,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Suspect apprehended at 1650 hours.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:39.51,0:19:43.63,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Why?! Satoru didn't do it!\NThere's no way he would have!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:43.63,0:19:44.75,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Satoru-san!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:45.66,0:19:51.22,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew that my relationship with Airi would\Ncease to be, either through arrest or Revival.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:51.70,0:19:54.78,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And now that time has come.\NI'll never see her again.
Dialogue: 10,0:19:55.50,0:19:57.06,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's something I have to do...
Dialogue: 10,0:19:57.06,0:19:59.47,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry, Satoru-san!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:59.47,0:20:05.82,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I probably led these people here, \Neven though I promised to come alone!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:06.30,0:20:09.28,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to give Airi what I wanted to give her.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:09.98,0:20:12.24,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just like she did for me.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:12.77,0:20:17.16,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry! So sorry! I'm so sorry...
Dialogue: 10,0:20:17.16,0:20:18.50,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's all my fault...
Dialogue: 10,0:20:19.66,0:20:23.05,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What would a superhero say at a time like this?
Dialogue: 10,0:20:26.81,0:20:30.01,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Isn't it hard to fight all alone?
Dialogue: 10,0:20:35.31,0:20:37.14,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,You've got it all wrong, Airi.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:37.56,0:20:39.39,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,It's because you believed in me...
Dialogue: 10,0:20:39.39,0:20:42.48,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,that I can keep fighting.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:43.23,0:20:46.36,GJM_Main,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Airi. I'm glad I believed in you.
